# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit anything that names a target.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The GitHub Pages CNAME file contains the victim hostname and would stay in
# the public git history forever. Ignored on purpose: the Vercel/Netlify flow
# keeps the hostname in the dashboard instead.
# Only if the dangling record points at *.github.io do you need it, and then:
#   git add -f CNAME
# ...accepting that the target is permanently disclosed in this repo.
/CNAME

# Screenshots, curl dumps, report drafts. These name the target. Keep them
# local, attach them to the report, never push them.
/evidence/
/screenshots/
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.webp
*.pdf
*.har

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Platform CLI state and secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vercel/
.netlify/
.wrangler/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
node_modules/
.cache/
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
